{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the development of a novel diazabenzacenaphthenium photoredox catalyst, NBAP, capable of promoting the multielectron (four-electron) reduction of esters. Using ammonium oxalate as a 'traceless reductant' under visible-light irradiation, the system generates carbinol anion intermediates that can be protonated to form alcohols or undergo 1,2-addition to carbonyl compounds to yield unsymmetric 1,2-diols.",
